// @check
// @error '__load_i32__' is a compiler intrinsic and cannot be redefined
// CONTRACT (must-error): the WORST failure class this compiler had — a SILENT WRONG
// ANSWER. `wasmEmit` dispatches on the CALLEE NAME before it looks up any declaration,
// so `__load_i32__(1)` lowered to an `i32.load` of address 1 and printed `0`: the user's
// function was silently discarded and `vl check` reported the program clean. The same
// held in statement position for `__store_i32__` and `__log__` (the body just vanished);
// the remaining intercepted names failed loudly only by ACCIDENT of stack shape, which a
// differently-shaped user signature would lose.
//
// The rule is the NAME, at the DEFINITION, where the author can see it — not the call
// site that quietly means something else. Reserved: `__store_i32__`, `__load_i32__`,
// `__log__`, `__trap__`, `__array_new__`, `__array_new_default__`, `__array_copy__`.
// A PARAMETER of that name is untouched (it is never a callee), and CALLING an intrinsic
// is of course still fine — see `intrinsics/array-new-fill.vl` and friends.
function __load_i32__(a: i32) {
  return 7
}
print(__load_i32__(1))
